    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100-a1">

                <pb facs="0162" n="90" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg90"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">circular</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-11-06"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Dean of diplomatic body to his
                        colleagues.</hi></p>
                <p>Carrying into effect the decision reached at the meeting of the diplomatic body
                    on the 1st instant, the dean yesterday went to the Wai-wu Pu to insist that the
                    dredging should be begun again without delay. His excellency, Mr. Liang Tun-yen,
                    promised to telegraph to Shanghai in this sense.</p>
                <p>As to the meaning of the last official note from the ministry of foreign affairs
                    of the 26th ultimo, transmitted to the diplomatic body by Circular 141, the
                    discussions had with Mr. Liang Tun-yen permit no doubt to remain but that the
                    Government believes itself freed from the obligations arising from the final
                    protocol with respect to the improvement of the Whangpoo. The said minister of
                    foreign affairs, nevertheless, recognized the necessity, and confirmed the
                    intention of the Chinese Government to continue the work of improvement, but in
                    its own right and in its own way.</p>
            </div>
